{"traj_id": "numina-24764_5", "problem": ", Given planar vectors $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}$ satisfy: $|\\vec{a}|=|\\vec{b}|, \\vec{c}=\\lambda \\vec{a}+\\mu \\vec{b},|\\vec{c}|=1+\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=$ $(\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c}=1$, try to find the minimum possible value of $\\frac{|\\vec{a}-\\vec{c}|}{|1+\\mu|}$.", "gold": "2-\\sqrt{2}", "pred": "0", "is_correct": false, "tier": "zero", "n_tokens": 8014, "meta_leak": [], "paragraphs": ["Let me carefully parse the problem. We have planar vectors $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}$ satisfying:\n1. $|\\vec{a}| = |\\vec{b}|$\n2. $\\vec{c} = \\lambda \\vec{a} + \\mu \\vec{b}$\n3. $|\\vec{c}| = 1 + \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = (\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c} = 1$", "Wait, let me re-read. The conditions are:\n- $|\\vec{a}| = |\\vec{b}|$\n- $\\vec{c} = \\lambda \\vec{a} + \\mu \\vec{b}$\n- $|\\vec{c}| = 1 + \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = (\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c} = 1$", "So this means:\n- $|\\vec{c}| = 1$\n- $1 + \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 1$, so $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 0$\n- $(\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c} = 1$", "Wait, let me re-read. \"$|\\vec{c}|=1+\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=$$(\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c}=1$\"", "So $|\\vec{c}| = 1 + \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = (\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c} = 1$", "This means all three expressions equal 1:\n- $|\\vec{c}| = 1$\n- $1 + \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 1$, so $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 0$\n- $(\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c} = 1$", "So we have:\n- $|\\vec{a}| = |\\vec{b}| = r$ (say)\n- $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 0$\n- $|\\vec{c}| = 1$\n- $(\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c} = 1$\n- $\\vec{c} = \\lambda \\vec{a} + \\mu \\vec{b}$", "Since $\\vec{a} \\perp \\vec{b}$ and $|\\vec{a}| = |\\vec{b}| = r$, let me set up coordinates.", "Let $\\vec{a} = (r, 0)$ and $\\vec{b} = (0, r)$.", "Then $\\vec{c} = \\lambda \\vec{a} + \\mu \\vec{b} = (\\lambda r, \\mu r)$.", "$|\\vec{c}| = 1$ gives $\\lambda^2 r^2 + \\mu^2 r^2 = 1$, so $r^2(\\lambda^2 + \\mu^2) = 1$.", "$(\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c} = 1$:\n$\\vec{a} + \\vec{b} = (r, r)$\n$(\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c} = (r, r) \\cdot (\\lambda r, \\mu r) = r^2(\\lambda + \\mu) = 1$", "So we have:\n- $r^2(\\lambda^2 + \\mu^2) = 1$\n- $r^2(\\lambda + \\mu) = 1$", "From these: $\\lambda^2 + \\mu^2 = \\lambda + \\mu$", "This means $\\lambda^2 - \\lambda + \\mu^2 - \\mu = 0$\n$(\\lambda - 1/2)^2 + (\\mu - 1/2)^2 = 1/2$", "Now I need to find the minimum of $\\frac{|\\vec{a} - \\vec{c}|}{|1 + \\mu|}$.", "$|\\vec{a} - \\vec{c}| = |(-\\lambda r + r, -\\mu r)|$... wait, let me recalculate.", "$\\vec{a} = (r, 0)$, $\\vec{c} = (\\lambda r, \\mu r)$", "$\\vec{a} - \\vec{c} = (r - \\lambda r, -\\mu r) = (r(1-\\lambda), -\\mu r)$", "$|\\vec{a} - \\vec{c}| = r\\sqrt{(1-\\lambda)^2 + \\mu^2}$", "So we need to minimize $\\frac{r\\sqrt{(1-\\lambda)^2 + \\mu^2}}{|1 + \\mu|}$", "From $r^2(\\lambda + \\mu) = 1$, we get $r = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\lambda + \\mu}}$.", "So the expression becomes:\n$\\frac{\\sqrt{(1-\\lambda)^2 + \\mu^2}}{\\sqrt{\\lambda + \\mu} \\cdot |1 + \\mu|}$", "We need to minimize this subject to $\\lambda^2 + \\mu^2 = \\lambda + \\mu$ and $\\lambda + \\mu > 0$ (for $r$ to be real).", "Let me use the constraint $\\lambda^2 + \\mu^2 = \\lambda + \\mu$.", "Let $s = \\lambda + \\mu$ and $p = \\lambda\\mu$. Then $\\lambda^2 + \\mu^2 = s^2 - 2p = s$, so $p = \\frac{s(s-1)}{2}$.", "The expression to minimize is:\n$\\frac{\\sqrt{(1-\\lambda)^2 + \\mu^2}}{\\sqrt{s} \\cdot |1 + \\mu|}$", "$(1-\\lambda)^2 + \\mu^2 = 1 - 2\\lambda + \\lambda^2 + \\mu^2 = 1 - 2\\lambda + s$", "Hmm, this is asymmetric in $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$ because of the numerator. Let me think differently.", "Let me parameterize. From $\\lambda^2 + \\mu^2 = \\lambda + \\mu$, let me set:\n$\\lambda = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cos\\theta$\n$\\mu = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sin\\theta$", "Then $s = \\lambda + \\mu = 1 + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\cos\\theta + \\sin\\theta) = 1 + \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/4)$", "Wait, $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\cos\\theta + \\sin\\theta) = \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/4)$", "So $s = 1 + \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/4)$.", "For $s > 0$, we need $\\sin(\\theta + \\pi/4) > -1$, which is always true except at one point.", "Actually, $s = 1 + \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/4) \\geq 0$, with equality when $\\sin(\\theta + \\pi/4) = -1$.", "For $r$ to be well-defined, we need $s > 0$, so $\\sin(\\theta + \\pi/4) > -1$.", "Now the expression is:\n$E = \\frac{\\sqrt{(1-\\lambda)^2 + \\mu^2}}{\\sqrt{s} \\cdot |1 + \\mu|}$", "Let me compute $(1-\\lambda)^2 + \\mu^2$:\n$= (1 - \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}})^2 + (\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}})^2$\n$= (\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}})^2 + (\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}})^2$\n$= \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{2}$\n$= \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta}{2} + \\frac{\\sin\\theta - \\cos\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}}$\n$= \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sin\\theta - \\cos\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}}$\n$= 1 + \\frac{\\sin\\theta - \\cos\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}}$\n$= 1 + \\sin(\\theta - \\pi/4)$", "So $(1-\\lambda)^2 + \\mu^2 = 1 + \\sin(\\theta - \\pi/4)$.", "Now $|1 + \\mu| = |1 + \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}}| = |\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}}|$", "Since $\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}} \\geq -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\approx -0.707$ and $\\frac{3}{2} = 1.5$, we have $1 + \\mu = \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}} \\geq \\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2} - 2}{2\\sqrt{2}} > 0$.", "So $|1 + \\mu| = 1 + \\mu = \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}}$.", "And $s = 1 + \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/4) = 1 + \\frac{\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta}{\\sqrt{2}}$.", "So the expression becomes:\n$E = \\frac{\\sqrt{1 + \\sin(\\theta - \\pi/4)}}{\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{\\sin\\theta 